and hints and a replant's guard alike, as the content it holds \(em never
rewriting it there, so a replant's checkout update refuses over one, naming
it.
.PP
A resume takes the rebase as it finds it in the worktree: continued there by
hand to its end, its result lands, judged as one the run continued itself;
quit or aborted there by hand, it lands nothing \(em
.B \-\-continue
refuses, naming the picks the result lacks, a pick git left out as emptied
counting as made,
.B \-\-status
gives a pause aborted there the same verdict, and
.B \-\-abort
clears the pause. An edit keeps its amend in the pause, so for one whose
replay was aborted there both name the way on instead: reset the worktree to
that amend, then
.BR \-\-continue .
A pause whose worktree is no longer a checkout of this repository resumes
nothing, and
.B \-\-abort
leaves whatever stands at its path, naming it. Every stop a rebase continued
there by hand passed counts as one the run paused at, for the guards below.
A rebase begun there by hand, rather than the run's own, is
refused in progress, and a replant finished by hand on any base but the
upstream it named lands nothing. Conflict markers are refused in a commit made
at the stop, or committed by a rebase continued or finished there by hand, as
in a staged file \(em the base marker a
.B diff3
or
.B zdiff3
conflict writes included \(em and the conflicted commit keeps its own
message byte for byte, a
.BR # \-led
line and trailing whitespace too, as does every commit a rebase\-based mode
replays.
.PP
Each stop names the commit it builds \(em for a fold, the target itself \(em
and its resolution is that commit's content, the later steps replaying their
own changes on top. A resolution taking in what a later commit changes, the
file as the tip holds it say, leaves the tip the same but that commit's
change emptied into the stop's: the landing refuses it, naming each later
commit that replayed without lines of its own change to a file a stop's
commit changes, whether it conflicted there or the resolution staged it
beside, where most of those lines, blank and punctuation\-only ones
aside, and ones the stop's own commit undoes, as a line it removes that the
later one adds, now sit in that stop's commit \(em a line the later commit
removed counting where that commit holds the line its hunk put in its place,
so a later edit of a single line counts whole, unless that commit, rebuilt,
still rewrites the line's place, its change rebased onto the stop's rather
than taken in \(em a partial take counts too,
in a reorder or move as in a fold, and for
a binary file a change gone whole whose very content that commit holds \(em and
.B \-\-abort
then a resolution to the commit's own content lands it, as does a commit
placed with
.B \-\-after
or
.B \-\-before
placed after the latest commit named instead, which the refusal names.
Only what the stop's
commit changes beyond its own pick and the fold or fixups in it counts, so a
